<!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//DITA Bootstrap//DTD DITA Bootstrap Topic//EN" "bootstrap-topic.dtd">
<topic id="specialization">
  <title>Specialization</title>
  <shortdesc>DITA Bootstrap provides a DTD specialization, so Bootstrap components can be authored as native DITA
    elements with specialized attributes instead of <xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt> values.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <metadata>
      <keywords>
        <indexterm>Specialization
          <indexterm>DTD</indexterm>
        </indexterm>
        <indexterm><xmlatt>class</xmlatt></indexterm>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
  </prolog>
  <body>

      <p>Specialization is the standard DITA mechanism for defining that an element type or attribute is derived from
        an ancestor type. Unlike generic XML, DITA formally records the parent-child relationship between element
        types, so a new element inherits the semantics and the processing behavior of the element it was derived
        from.</p>
      <p>Information architects use specialization to define new kinds of information while maximizing reuse and
        minimizing maintenance costs. It is appropriate when existing elements cannot express the semantics you need
        or when the output requires specialized processing.</p>
     
      <p>The <xmlatt>class</xmlatt> attribute records each element's ancestry, mapping its current name to its more
        general equivalents. A processor that does not recognize a specialized element can therefore fall back to the
        base element it was derived from.</p>

    <section>
      <title>Why use a Bootstrap specialization</title>
      <p>Without specialization, a Bootstrap component is authored by adding <xmlatt>outputclass</xmlatt> values to
        generic DITA elements. The DITA Bootstrap DTD instead provides native DITA elements with specialized
        attributes for Bootstrap styling. The markup describes the component, and the specialization carries the
        Bootstrap-specific details.</p>
      <codeblock outputclass="language-xml">&lt;card color="primary" border="1" rounded="yes"&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;Card Title&lt;/title&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Card content goes here.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/card&gt;</codeblock>
    </section>
    <section>
      <title>Using the DTD</title>
      <p>Topics that use the specialized elements must declare the DITA Bootstrap DTD in the document type
        declaration:</p>
      <codeblock
        outputclass="language-xml"
      >&lt;!DOCTYPE topic PUBLIC "-//DITA Bootstrap//DTD DITA Bootstrap Topic//EN" "bootstrap-topic.dtd"&gt;</codeblock>
    </section>
